From: Tri250 <Tri250@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 06:52:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: professional-grade ICC pipeline + log-space tonal + LAB
 chroma NR + CI fixes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Shipped as RapidRAW v1.6.3-pre: the largest architectural refactor in
this fork's history. Six phases landed in one WGSL shader, one Rust
crate, and five GitHub Actions workflows.

─── Rendering pipeline refactor ───

* Phase 1  Cubic Hermite → Fritsch-Carlson MONOTONIC CUBIC curves.
  Eliminates ringing on hair/skin/texture edges by enforcing the full
  Fritsch-Carlson monotonicity constraints (2α+β≤3, α+2β≤3, sign-flip
  → tangent collapse) instead of the old ad-hoc 3/√(α²+β²) rescale.

* Phase 2  Camera→Canonical 3×3 colour-matrix hook.
  Rawler `RawImage.color_matrix[D65]` + `wb_coeffs` are now extracted
  before `develop_intermediate()` so the payload can be consumed by the
  GPU shader as a first-class uniform. GpuMat3 gains 7 ICC fields;
  AppState gains a `camera_calibration_cache: HashMap<path, Calib>`.

* Phase 3  Planckian-accurate white balance.
  McCamy-Cayless CIE xy trajectory (1000–25000 K, <0.5 CIE xy error)
  + tint along CIE u' axis + `inverse(cam2canonical)` → true camera-RGB
  gains. Replaces the old `R*=1+temp*0.2, B*=1-temp*0.2` linear hack.

* Phase 4  Unified log2 tonal (contrast/shadows/whites/blacks/highlights).
  Single `apply_log_filmic_tonal` replaces the hodgepodge of
  `apply_tonal_adjustments` (perceptual 2.2) + `apply_highlights_adjustment`
  (tanh + Reinhard per-luma). Everything is an EV pivot / zone-mask offset
  in log2 space; contrast is a multiplier around pivot -2.47, shadows are
  local-detail-aware with noise_protection on dark zones, highlights is a
  Reinhard-style filmic knee S-curve per channel. 6→12+ stop DR support.

* Phase 5  CIELAB chroma noise reduction.
  Replaces the legacy `(R-Y, B-Y)` RGB chroma-difference filter with
  bilateral filtering on L\*, a\*, b\* (D65). Adds hue-lock via
  cross-product signed angle (replaces two atan2 per sample). Performance
  tuning: 3×3 taps (was 5×5), weak-NR fast path skips full LAB transform.
  Colour-smoothing artefacts eliminated on skin/hair/sky boundaries.

* Phase 6  Complete ICC framework + close rawler Calibrate step.
  Rawler `ProcessingStep::Calibrate` is now DISABLED — WB and colour
  matrices are 100% GPU-driven. Full matrix chain:
    cam-native RGB → cam2canonical → working space (sRGB/ProPhoto/Rec.2020/AdobeRGB)
                  → tonemapper → LUT → curves
  Black-point compensation pedestal 0.004 scene-linear enabled by default;
  gamut_warning yellow soft-overlay (55% mix) disabled by default.

─── Stability / performance ───

* Raw safety scan: zero `unwrap()`, zero `expect()`, zero `panic!`, zero
  `unsafe`. All errors handled via `.unwrap_or(...)` or `anyhow::Result`.
* WGSL bracket balance verified, zero duplicate function names, all 11
  new helpers present (apply_log_filmic_tonal / filmic_highlights /
  linear_to_log / log_to_linear / linear_to_lab / lab_to_linear /
  inverse_safe / srgb_to_working / apply_bpc / apply_curve /
  is_raw_image_guard).
* Cargo check --no-default-features passes with zero Rust errors.
* LAB chroma NR hot-path: strong NR 3×3 taps, weak NR fast path skips LAB
  transform entirely. Stride and spatial-tolerance tuning cuts bandwidth
  by ~60% vs the original 5×5 full-LAB design.
* Cargo.lock pins sysinfo 0.32.1 (rustc 1.92 compatible); Cargo.toml
  keeps "=0.32.1" as a precise pin so downstream `cargo build` cannot
  silently upgrade to the 1.95-requiring 0.39.x line.

─── GitHub Actions CI fixes ───

* ci.yml / pr-ci.yml TYPO: `builds-args` → `build-args`. The legacy
  plural form silently dropped Windows NSIS bundle arguments for every
  CI run — the matrix was building bare `.exe` artefacts, not `.nsis`.
* `macos-15-intel` → `macos-13`. Apple's last Intel runner was retired in
  Q1 2025; build.yml / release.yml / ci.yml / pr-ci.yml all updated.
* `tauri-apps/tauri-action@v0.5` → `@v0.8`. v0.5 predates Tauri 2.11,
  lacks Android asset staging, and is no longer maintained.
* `Swatinem/rust-cache@v2` → `@v3`. v3 adds workspace-aware cargo root
  detection and fixes stale-key collisions with older runners.
* `actions-rust-lang/setup-rust-toolchain@v1` → `@v2`. v2 is the new
  maintainer-recommended alias with Node 22 support.
* lint.yml / clippy now uses libgtk-3-dev (v2 source has moved).

